; --verify traces the construction and destruction of Ledger's objects
; and, once the session has been torn down, reports on stderr any still
; alive.  Adding a commodity that a balance does not yet hold must leave
; none behind: the euro of the second transaction turns the totals of
; Assets:Cash and Income:Gift, and the grand total, into balances of two
; commodities, and the test expects nothing on stderr.  A balance that
; built the new component from a static default value would keep that
; value alive past the report.
;
; Only Debug builds trace objects.  In a Release build --verify has no
; effect, and this test checks only the balance report.

2024/01/01 Dollar
    Assets:Cash        $1
    Income:Gift

2024/01/02 Euro
    Assets:Cash        1 EUR
    Income:Gift

test --verify bal
                  $1
               1 EUR  Assets:Cash
                 $-1
              -1 EUR  Income:Gift
--------------------
                   0
end test
